note Translation of the inner function _ignore_patterns from CPython's shutil.ignore_patterns (Lib/shutil.py).
note In Python it is a closure: ignore_patterns(*patterns) returns _ignore_patterns, which captures patterns and is later called by copytree as ignore(path, names).
note GAP: closure capturing an outer variable - the doc has no nested operations, no operation values and no capture, so `patterns` becomes an explicit parameter. copytree can then no longer accept an arbitrary ignore callable, and nothing here says how one is stored or passed.

note fnmatch.filter: the names that match pattern.
to fnmatch_filter names by pattern using memory
    given names is a List of Text
    given pattern is Text
    given memory is an Allocator
    produces a List of Text
    fails with OutOfMemory
    uses memory

note GAP: Python's set type - the doc has no Set collection. `Set of Text` and `set_of` are guessed.
to set_of items using memory
    given items is a List of Text
    given memory is an Allocator
    produces a Set of Text
    fails with OutOfMemory
    uses memory

to ignore_patterns_for path and names with patterns using memory
    given path is Text
    given names is a List of Text
    given patterns is a List of Text
    given memory is an Allocator
    produces a Set of Text
    fails with OutOfMemory
    uses memory
    note path is unused, as in the original. copytree's callback protocol passes it.

    var ignored_names starts at []
    for each pattern in patterns
        let matched be try fnmatch_filter names by pattern using memory
        note GAP: list.extend has no form in the doc. Only `append value to list` (example 9) and `followed by` (in specs) exist, so `followed by` is used in code here.
        set ignored_names to ignored_names followed by matched
    give back try set_of ignored_names using memory
